@[expose] public section

/-!
# The oscillation gauges of `e.BoscL.def` are integral-local

`Algsuperdiff.Section3.Provider.BadEvents.LocalMeasurability` places the
*pointwise* data of a shell field — its values and its directional first
derivatives — in the integral-generated local sigma-field
`ShellField.lihLocalSigma U`.  The gauges of `e.BoscL.def` are suprema of such
pointwise data over the open cube, so two further steps are needed.

* The stored **second** derivative is recovered from first derivatives by the
  same difference-quotient limit, and a continuous linear map out of
  `Vec d = Fin d → ℝ` is recovered from its values on the standard basis
  through `ContinuousLinearEquiv.piRing`.  This gives
  `ShellField.secondDeriv j x` as a `lihLocalSigma U`-measurable function of
  `j`.
* The supremum over the *uncountable* open cube is replaced by a supremum over
  a *countable dense* subset.  This is legitimate because the sharp
  characterizations `unitCubeDerivNorm_le_iff` and
  `unitCubeSecondDerivNorm_le_iff'` identify the unit-cube norms as the least
  nonnegative constants dominating a continuous function on the open cube.

The conclusion is that the single-shell oscillation gauge `shellOscGauge Q L`
reads the shell `j_L` only on the closed cube `z + \bar{square}_j`: it is
measurable for the sigma-field generated by the `L`-th shell coordinate with
its `lihLocalSigma`-structure on any `U` containing that closed cube.

## Main results

* `measurable_eval_deriv_lihLocalSigma`, `measurable_eval_secondDeriv_lihLocalSigma`:
  the stored derivatives at an interior point are integral-local, as operators.
* `unitCubeDerivNorm_eq_iSup`, `unitCubeSecondDerivNorm_eq_iSup`: the unit-cube
  gauges are countable suprema over a dense subset of the open cube.
* `measurable_localCubeDerivNorm_translate_lihLocalSigma`,
  `measurable_localCubeSecondDerivNorm_translate_lihLocalSigma`: the two `L^∞`
  gauges of the translated shell at scale `ell` are `lihLocalSigma U`-measurable
  whenever `U` contains the closed ball of radius `3^ell / 2` around the base
  point, i.e. the closed cube `z + \bar{square}_{ell}`.
* `measurable_shellOscGauge_shellLocal`, `measurableSet_badOscAt_shellLocal`:
  the `e.BoscL.def` gauge and event at shell index `L` are measurable for the
  `L`-th shell coordinate's integral-local sigma-field on the closed cube.

## References

* ABK26, `e.BoscL.def`.
* ABK26 (the volume-normalized Sobolev norm).
-/

namespace Algsuperdiff.Section3.Provider.BadEvents

open Filter MeasureTheory Topology
open HCPolySupport
open scoped Matrix.Norms.Elementwise
